@Commands
อออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออ
ÛÛ ÛÛ ÛÛ ÞÛÛÝ ÛÛÛÛÛÛÜ ÜÛÛÛÛÛÛ       Version 4 Revision 0
ÛÛ ÛÛ ÛÛ  ÛÛ  ÛÛÜÜÜÛÛ ÛÛÜÜÜÜ       (c) Copyright 1994-1997
ÛÛ ÛÛ ÛÛ  ÛÛ  ÛÛ฿฿฿฿  ÛÛ฿฿฿฿                 by
฿ÛÛÛÛÛÛ฿ ÞÛÛÝ ÛÛ      ฿ÛÛÛÛÛÛ      De Trans Software (DTS)
อออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออ

  WIPE is a program tha allows you to destroy files
completely.

  USAGE: WIPED <Mask> [Options] [Method]

         <Mask>
         Is a valid DOS mask, it may include wildcards and
         paths. Eg: *.*, C:\DOS\*.COM, ..\*.??A

         [Options]
         They are optional.
         Are valid switches that modifies WIPE defaults.
         You can activate one switch ending it with a + or
         deactivate it ending int with a -.
         Options suported are listed these:
         /386:      Use 386 instructions (Registered only).
                    WIPE will use 386 or later features if
                    available.
         /EMS:      Use EMS memory (Registered only).
                    WIPE will use EMS memory if available.
         /DIRECT:   Use direct output.
                    WIPE will perform direct screen output.
         /SOUND:    Enable sound.
                    WIPE will enable system sounds.
         /STACKER:  Duplicator tolerance.
                    WIPE will use Stacker/Super Stor/Double
                    Space compatibility.
         /SLACK:    Clear slack.
                    WIPE will clear the slack of each file.
         /FAT:      Clear FAT.
                    WIPE will clear the FAT.
         /TOTAL     Total confirmation.
                    WIPE will ask you before deleting
                    files.
         /ATTRIB:   Attrib confirmation.
                    WIPE will ask you before deleting an
                    attributed file.
         /FILE:     File confirmation.
                    WIPE will ask you before deleteing each
                    file.
         /CANCEL:   Cancel confirmation.
                    WIPE will ask you after cancelling the
                    process.
         /SAVE      Autosave options.
                    WIPE will save automatically the
                    configuration.

         [Method]
         It is optional.
         Are valid switches that modifies WIPE default
         destruction method.
         /STANDARD: Use Standard method.
                    WIPE will use the DOS standard deletion
                    method.
         /FAST:     Use Fast method.
                    WIPE will use the fast wipe method.
         /SAFE:     Use Safe method.
                    WIPE will use the safe wipe method.
         /SECURE:   Use Secure method.
                    WIPE will use the secure method.
         /NCSA:     Use NCSA method (Registered only).
                    WIPE will use the secure wipe method.
@

