@Methods
ษอออออออออออ Configure Method อออออออออออออออป
บ     Which method of destruction do you     บÛÛ
บ              want to use?                  บÛÛ
บ                                            บÛÛ
บ               ( ) Standard                 บÛÛ
บ               ( ) Fast                     บÛÛ
บ               ( ) Safe                     บÛÛ
บ               ( ) Secure                   บÛÛ
บ               ( ) NCSA                     บÛÛ
ศออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออผÛÛ
  ÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛ

  WIPE has different ways of destroying a file:

  þ Standard: This is the DOS standard method (commonly
              used by DEL, ERASE, and so on).
  þ Fast:     This method overwrites the FAT allocation for
              the file to be destroyed.
  þ Secure:   This method overwrites the FAT allocation and
              the header of the file to be destroyed.
  þ Safe:     This method overwrites the FAT allocation and
              the complete image of the file to be
              destroyed.
  þ NCSA:     This method overwrites the FAT allocation and
              the complete image of the file to be
              destroyed using the NCSA (National Computer
              Security Association) method.
              Only available in the registered version.

  The methods are sorted by speed (from fast to slow), and
by security (from less to more).

  Recomended method is Safe for its balance between speed
and security.

  You can switch between methods using TAB and Shift-TAB,
activate/deactivate one using SPACE or INS, and accept
current selections with ENTER.
@

@Options
ษอออออออออออ Configure Options ออออออออออออออป
บ         Please set default WIPE            บÛÛ
บ                 options                    บÛÛ
บ                                            บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Use 386 instructions           บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Use EMS memory                 บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Use EMS memory                 บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Enable sound                   บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Duplicator tolerance           บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Clear slack                    บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Clear FAT                      บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Total confirmation             บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Attrib confirmation            บÛÛ
บ         [ ] File confirmation              บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Cancel confirmation            บÛÛ
บ         [ ] Autosave options               บÛÛ
ศออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออผÛÛ
  ÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛÛ

  WIPE has different general settings that modifies its
general comportament:

  þ Use 386 Instructions: This will allow WIPE to use
                          enhaced 386 or latter
                          instructions if available,
                          getting more execution speed. We
                          recommend to activate this
                          option.
                          Only available in the registered
                          version.
  þ Use EMS memory:       This will allow WIPE to use EMS
                          memory if available getting more
                          execution speed. We recommend to
                          activate this option.
                          Only available in the registered
                          version.
  þ Use direct output:    This will allow WIPE to use
                          direct to screen output in front
                          of BIOS output. Direct output is
                          faster, but BIOS are more
                          compatible. We recommend to
                          activate this option.
  þ Enable sound:         This will allow WIPE to produce
                          system sounds.
  þ Duplicator tolerance: This will allow WIPE to destroy
                          files using a compatibility
                          method for Stacker, Super Stor,
                          Double Space, Double Disk, ...
                          (This option is not compatible
                          with the NCSA wiping method).
  þ Clear slack:          This will allow WIPE to clear the
                          slack data of each file (data at
                          the end of a sector that not
                          necessarily pertains to the file.
  þ Clear FAT:            This will allow WIPE to clear the
                          FAT (File Alocation Table) of
                          each file.
  þ Total confirmation:   This will ask you before start
                          wipping.
  þ Attrib confirmation:  This will ask you before start
                          wipping on file that has special
                          attributtes (Read-Only, System,
                          or Hidden).
  þ File confirmation:    This will ask you before start
                          wipping one file.
  þ Cancel confirmation:  This will ask you before
                          cancelling the wipping process.
  þ Autosave options:     This will automatically save the
                          settings of WIPE each time they
                          are modified in a file called
                          WIPED.CFG.

  You can switch between options using TAB and Shift-TAB,
activate/deactivate one using SPACE or INS, and accept
current selections with ENTER.
@

